Operating Expense Scaling:
• Technology: 30% of revenue (R&D investment)
• Sales & Marketing: 20% of revenue (growth investment)
• G&A: 12% of revenue (operational scaling)
• Customer Success: 8% of revenue (retention focus)

Break-Even Calculation Methodology:
• Operating break-even: Revenue > Operating Expenses
• Cash flow break-even: Positive monthly cash generation
• Debt service coverage: Revenue supports 18% payment + operations
• All calculations use conservative revenue projections

Debt Service Mathematical Verification:
• Total Debt: $5,600,000 ($4M principal + $1.6M ROI)
• 18% of $3.167M = $570,060 monthly (Months 19-24)
• 18% of $10.833M = $1,950,000 monthly (Month 25)
• Final payment Month 26: $229,640 (remaining balance)
• Total payments: $5,600,000 (exactly matches debt obligation)

The financial model has been stress-tested across multiple scenarios and demonstrates robust performance under conservative assumptions while providing substantial upside potential for both investor returns and founder value creation.